---
kind: lore
id: talks
title: Everyday moments around the station
---

// Repeatable conversations: whoever is in the room when you walk in.
// The bigger scenes (scenes/sol, scenes/wren) outrank these by priority.

<beat id="solRadio" on="visit" target="place.radio" title="Sol at the set" priority="10" once="false" after="visited('sol.first')" when="holds(at(sol, radio))">
  ::bg{location="radio_room" time="morning"}
  ::use{component="enter" who="sol" side="right"}
  @sol{emotion="tired"}: Morning. The night was a trawler, two ham operators in Tromsø, and a man who thinks the moon is a transmitter.
  <hub id="radioHub" prompt="Sol pushes a chair at you with his foot.">
    <choice id="listen" label="Put on the spare headphones" once>
      @narrator: Static, then a voice reading shipping weather in a language you don't speak, calm as a lullaby.
      @sol{emotion="fond"}: Nice, right? Nobody's listening but us.
    </choice>
    <choice id="wire" label="Ask for some wire for Wren's lantern" once when="quest.lantern.state == 'active' && !holds(carrying(wire))">
      ::gather{part="wire"}
      @sol{emotion="surprised"}: The goat girl? Take the copper, the good stuff. Tell her it's on loan from the sky.
    </choice>
    <choice id="leave" label="Leave him to it" exit>
      @sol: Go on. The sky's all yours till seven.
    </choice>
  </hub>
</beat>

<beat id="solRoofIdle" on="visit" target="place.roof" title="Sol on the roof" priority="0" once="false" after="visited('sol.first')" when="holds(at(sol, roof))">
  ::bg{location="roof" time="night"}
  ::use{component="enter" who="sol"}
  @sol{emotion="happy"}: Vega, Deneb, Altair. The Summer Triangle. Every year it comes back like it forgot something.
</beat>

// Sol warms once a day, wherever the player finds him: the radio room in the
// morning or the roof at night. One beat over every place, read per member.
<beat id="solWarm" on="visit" target="kind:place" title="Sol saves you something" also once="day" after="visited('sol.first')" when="holds(at(sol, occasion.target))">
  <match on="occasion.target">
    <when is="radio">
      @narrator: Sol slides the good headphones over without looking up.
    </when>
    <when is="roof">
      @narrator: Sol shifts over and gives you half the blanket.
    </when>
    // Only the village is left (festival night, on his route). The checker
    // still asks for deck and kitchen, where Sol never is.
    <otherwise>
      @narrator: Sol saves you the bench under the one lantern that isn't swinging.
    </otherwise>
  </match>
  ::set{run.aff.sol += 1}
</beat>

<beat use="inesAt" id="inesDeck" title="Ines at the instruments" where="deck" bg="deck" time="morning" side="left">
  @ines{emotion="neutral"}: You're hovering. Either read the anemometer or hand me that pencil.
  @ines{emotion="neutral" when="run.readings >= 1 && run.readings < 3"}: {{run.readings:plural(One careful morning|# careful mornings)}} in the log. Keep going.
  @ines{emotion="fond" when="run.readings >= 3"}: Your columns are getting neat. Don't let it go to your head.
</beat>

<beat use="inesAt" id="inesRadio" title="Ines with the charts" where="radio" bg="radio_room" time="afternoon" side="left">
  @ines{emotion="stern"}: Charts. Isobars. Don't touch the pins.
  @ines{emotion="worried" when="quest.forecast.state == 'active' && !run.forecastWritten && run.readings < 2"}: I can't sign a forecast off one morning of your numbers. Give me a few careful readings first.
</beat>

<beat use="inesAt" id="inesSupper" title="Ines at supper" priority="10" where="kitchen" bg="kitchen" time="night">
  @ines{emotion="tired"}: There's more lentils. There is always more lentils.
  <branch id="supper" prompt="She's darning a sock with the concentration of a surgeon.">
    <choice id="candle" label="Ask whether the station has a slow candle" when="quest.lantern.state == 'active' && !holds(carrying(candle))">
      ::gather{part="candle"}
      @ines{emotion="fond"}: Storm candles. Third drawer. They burn nine hours; I timed one in 1998 during the long blackout.
      @ines: Tell Wren's mother I said hello. She'll know what it means.
    </choice>
    <choice id="chat" label="Ask how long she's been up here">
      @ines{emotion="neutral"}: Twenty-six summers. I came as an intern. The brochure lied to me too.
    </choice>
  </branch>
</beat>

<beat id="pellPost" on="visit" target="place.kitchen" title="Pell with the post" priority="20" once="false" when="holds(at(pell, kitchen))">
  ::bg{location="kitchen" time="morning"}
  ::use{component="enter" who="pell" side="right"}
  @pell{emotion="happy"}: Post! Two letters for Ines, a catalogue for Sol, and nothing for you, because nobody knows you're up here yet.
  <branch id="post" prompt="Pell is already eyeing the teapot.">
    <choice id="paper" label="Ask if he has any strong paper" when="quest.lantern.state == 'active' && !holds(carrying(paper))">
      ::gather{part="paper"}
      @pell{emotion="laughing"}: For Wren's lantern? Everyone's asking. Here — waxed parcel paper. Won't tear in a gale.
    </choice>
    <choice id="tea" label="Offer him tea">
      @pell: Now you're talking. Three sugars, it's a steep road.
    </choice>
  </branch>
</beat>

<beat id="wrenLantern" on="visit" target="place.village" title="Working on the lantern" priority="10" once="false" after="visited('wren.first')" when="holds(at(wren, village))">
  ::bg{location="village_pen" time="afternoon"}
  ::use{component="enter" who="wren" side="left"}
  <match on="quest.lantern.state">
    <when is="active" test="count(carrying(_)) >= 3">
      @wren{emotion="laughing"}: That's everything! Oh, it's going to fly. Well. Float. Hover with conviction.
    </when>
    <when is="active">
      @wren{emotion="happy"}: You came back! Hold this end. No, the other end. The end that's an end.
      @wren{emotion="worried"}: Still missing some bits. Paper, wire, candle — the shop still only sells postcards.
    </when>
    <when is="complete">
      @wren{emotion="fond"}: I keep checking it's still on the windowsill. It is. It's very patient.
    </when>
    <otherwise>
      @wren{emotion="neutral"}: Hello, station intern. The goats say hello. Well. They say "meh."
    </otherwise>
  </match>
</beat>

// The first time each day the player comes down to the pen, Wren warms a
// little — once a day, not once a visit. Rides along with whatever plays there.
<beat id="wrenWarm" on="visit" target="place.village" title="Wren saves you the sunny end" also once="day" after="visited('wren.first')" when="holds(at(wren, village))">
  @narrator: Wren shifts along the fence to give you the sunny end.
  ::set{run.aff.wren += 1}
</beat>
